Forbrickit — a hardcore unified Minecraft server: Fabric + Forge + NeoForge mods
and Bukkit/Paper plugins in one instance
Copyright 2026 The Forbrickit Project

Forbrickit is a fork of Forbric
(https://github.com/Ray-T-r/Minecraft-Forbric-mod-loader), which is a clean-room
unified Minecraft mod loader. The name is the four ecosystems it unifies:
`for` + `(fa)bric` + `(neo)bric` + `(buk)kit`. The upstream project unifies three
of them; this fork adds the fourth, Paper's Bukkit API, through a bridge carried
on the game side of the kernel.

This fork is SERVER-SIDE ONLY. It builds a server; Bukkit and Paper are server
APIs and a player's client installs nothing for them. The upstream client code is
still present in this tree — it has not been removed, because this fork adapts
the server side and the client is out of scope — but it is unmaintained here and
its behaviour is not guaranteed. A client built from this fork's source may
behave in ways nobody has tested. Build the Forbric client from the Forbric
repository instead.

Upstream copyright and licence are unchanged: this fork is distributed under the
same Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE), and the modules below keep the
provenance they had upstream.

